        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="d162-6" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve14p1/pgd162-6"/>

                <head>163. Telegram 9875 From the Embassy in Rome to the Department of State, June
                    17, 1976, 0844Z.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d163-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d163-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Rome</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1976-06-17T08:44:00+00:00">June 17, 1976, 0844Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d163-1" n="1" xml:id="pgd163-1"/>
                <pb facs="d163-2" n="2" xml:id="pgd163-2"/>
                <p>TELEGRAM <lb/> Department of State<lb/>ROME 9878</p>
                <p>P R 170844Z JUN 76</p>
                <p>FM AMEMBASSY ROME<lb/>TO SECSTATE WASHDC PRIORITY 8320<lb/>INFO USMISSION USUN
                    NEW YORK</p>
                <p>ROME 9875</p>
                <p> FODAG <lb/> FROM SISCO <lb/> DEPT PASS ASST SEC ROGERS </p>
                <p>11652: GDS<lb/>TAGS: OCON, FAO.</p>
                <p>SUBJECT: 2ND WORLD FOOD COUNCIL</p>
                <p>1. U.S. ACHIEVED ITS OBJECTIVES IN WFC BY GETTING ENDORSEMENT OF PREPCOM
                    RECOMMENDATION AND PREVENTING ENDORSEMENT OF ALL FIVE GROUP-77 RESOLUTIONS, ALL
                    OF WHICH WERE SUBSTANTIVELY UNACCEPTABLE TO US.</p>
                <p>2. THIS POSITIVE OUTCOME WAS A RESULT OF: </p>
                <p>A) STRONG OECD GROUP SUPPORT OF EQUALLY STRONG U.S. LEAD IN ALL CONSULTATIONS
                    WITH THEM. WE ACHIEVED A SOLID, UNITED FRONT WITH PRINCIPAL AGRICULTURAL
                    PRODUCERS BY MEETING TWICE A DAY WITH GROUP AND CONCERTING STRATEGY EVERY STEP
                    OF WAY. UK, AUSTRALIA, FRG AND JAPAN PARTICULARLY HELPFUL AND </p>
                <p>B) EXTENSIVE U.S. CONSULTATION WITH CERTAIN KEY G-77 DELS SUCCEEDED IN WEAKENING
                    GUINEA AND MEXICAN LEADERSHIP IN GROUP AND FINALLY ISOLATING THEM. VOLPE</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Foreign Policy Files, D760233–1134.
                    Confidential; Priority. Repeated to USUN.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p> Sisco reported success in promoting U.S. objectives at the Second World Food
                    Council.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
